# pocket_floor_offset.cam — a pocket's floor finished to size by its own op (Phase 27
# slice 4; DECISIONS.md → "Phase 27 slice 4: the floor's verb…").
#
# `Floor` finishes a declared planar floor to its declared height, and a
# pocket declares one. So the floor has a verb, and the three verbs never
# compete because each names a different surface of the same feature:
#
#   Clear   the VOLUME   — roughed, leaving 0.5 on every surface it touches
#   Floor  the FLOOR    — taken to z=-6, standing 0.5 off the walls
#   Finish  the WALL     — taken to size, full depth
#
# There is still ONE allowance. `stock_to_leave=0.5` on the Clear is the
# radial skin it always was; it is left on the FLOOR as well only because the
# Floor below is there to take it — delete that line and the same Clear cuts
# its floor to size, as every pocket roughed before this rule still does. The
# program says which: "(floor: 0.500 left for the Floor op that follows)".
#
# The Floor's own stock_to_leave is its stand-off from the walls, so the floor
# pass does not rub a wall the Finish has yet to take; the post in the middle
# is an island of the floor exactly as it is of the volume.
units mm
feed 800
plunge 300
rapid_z 5
clearance_z 25
spindle 3000

stock Box(w=100, l=80, h=20, x=0, y=0, z=0)

tool T5 Endmill(dia=10.0)

feature Cavity ProfilePocket(extent=6.0
    15 15
    85 15
    85 65
    15 65
)

feature Post CylinderBoss(dia=14, extent=6, x=50, y=40, z=-6)

run Clear(tool=T5, profile=Cavity, stepover=4.0, stock_to_leave=0.5)
run End(tool=T5, surface=Cavity, stepover=4.0, stock_to_leave=0.5, pattern=offset)
run Side(tool=T5, surface=Cavity)
run Side(tool=T5, surface=Post, stepover=6.0)
